 "old_transcript": "(Note: The prompt designates Level T2, which maps to the B1-B2 intermediate tier defined in the guidelines).\n\nOrgan donation is a vital medical process that can save lives. When a person decides to become a donor, they give permission for their healthy organs to be used if they pass away. Sometimes, a living donor can also give part of an organ, like a kidney, to help a relative or friend. \n\nThe organ transplant procedure requires a skilled team of doctors. First, they carefully test the organ to make sure it is safe. Then, they use surgery to place the healthy organ into the patient who needs it. This medical step gives many people a second chance at life because their bodies can work well again.",
